Your assignment: <%= it.instruction %>
Why it is needed: <%= it.reason %>

All input documents remain available in the inherited context. Work from their actual contents, including any accepted prerequisite findings. Revisit exact passages with grep, search and read_file when needed. Use arithmetic for numerical calculations. For enumeration/ranking, check the entire relevant set and all exclusions; don't mistake a partial list for an exhaustive answer.

When finished, CALL report. finding should preserve the useful conclusion, calculation or candidate answer. evidence identifies exact passages using one-based document, startLine and endLine from read_file; the harness copies the original source text. Do not invent line numbers: read the passage first. Choose compact ranges with necessary headings, row labels, dates and units (8-1600 characters each, at most 100 lines). uncertainty states missing evidence or disagreements; empty only when supported. Do not put tool markup inside field values. If no passage supports a claim, omit that evidence and explicitly state the uncertainty. Keep the report focused on this assignment, not a general document summary.

Stay within the assigned subproblem; do not independently answer other workers' assignments unless yours explicitly requires combining them. For a number, preserve its exact row/metric label, column date, unit and population with the value. Read nearby labels and totals to distinguish similar metrics, subtotals and consolidated totals; a matching number without the right label is not evidence. A supporting range must include the claimed fact, not just nearby text.

For percentages, state what each numerator and denominator counts. Distinguish a conditional share of a subgroup from the subgroup's share of the entire population. Combine percentages only when their populations actually nest, use arithmetic for the calculation, and round only the final requested result. Do not multiply incompatible denominators merely because two percentages appear together.
